From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: a disc's time is the picture's at a title change
 and in a menu

Around a disc's change of title the time shown went wrong for several
seconds: a total of -589 s on a 512 s title, a 118 s trailer counting 28
seconds in four, a film opening at 56 s before falling back to 11 s.
Nothing was skipped; UpdatePlayState() reported times the picture did not
have.

When the reader reaches the end of a title the disc has no title info,
so no total, and the full update falls back to a start and an end both
equal to the time. The update made while the old title plays out then
copies that state and replaces only the time and the end, so the stale
start stays, and the total, end minus start, goes negative until the
next full update. It now starts from zero, as the full update does.

In a menu, and a BD-J disc counts as one whenever its graphics plane is
up, which covers the trailers it plays, the time was replaced by the
input's time: the read position, which runs ahead while the queue fills
and crawls once it is full. A time computed from the picture on screen
is now kept, and the read position is used only when there is none.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
index d4046b681f..8afcd249ed 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -5948,6 +5948,7 @@ void CVideoPlayer::UpdatePlayState(double timeout)
       return;
     SPlayerState state(m_State);
     state.time = DVD_TIME_TO_MSEC(m_clock.GetClock() + offset);
+    state.timeMin = 0;
     state.timeMax = totalTime;
     if (m_Edl.HasCuts())
     {
@@ -5958,6 +5959,7 @@ void CVideoPlayer::UpdatePlayState(double timeout)
     m_processInfo->SetPlayTimes(state.startTime, state.time, state.timeMin, state.timeMax);
     std::unique_lock lock(m_StateSection);
     m_State.time = state.time;
+    m_State.timeMin = state.timeMin;
     m_State.timeMax = state.timeMax;
     return;
   }
@@ -5984,6 +5986,7 @@ void CVideoPlayer::UpdatePlayState(double timeout)
   std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream::IMenus> pMenu = std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDVDInputStream::IMenus>(m_pInputStream);
 
   bool chapterNbEnabled{false};
+  bool pictureTime{false};
 
   if (m_pDemuxer)
   {
@@ -6128,6 +6131,7 @@ void CVideoPlayer::UpdatePlayState(double timeout)
       m_displayTime.Get(clock, offset, totalTime);
       state.time += offset * 1000 / DVD_TIME_BASE;
       state.timeMax = totalTime;
+      pictureTime = true;
     }
     else
     {
@@ -6150,7 +6154,8 @@ void CVideoPlayer::UpdatePlayState(double timeout)
       }
       else if (IsInMenuInternal())
       {
-        state.time = pDisplayTime->GetTime();
+        if (!pictureTime)
+          state.time = pDisplayTime->GetTime();
         state.isInMenu = true;
         if (!pMenu->CanSeek())
           state.time_offset = 0;
